<figure id="S5.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S5.T3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="S5.T3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Comparison of HollowFlow trained using different <math id="S5.T3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>NN graphs and the non-hollow fully connected baseline, all trained on LJ55. The two rightmost columns show the effective speed-up compared to the baseline <a href="#S5.E21" title="In Criteria to Assess Effectiveness ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ HollowFlow: Efficient Sample Likelihood Evaluation using Hollow Message Passing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a> with and without weight clipping. Bold indicates best performance.</span></figcaption>
