<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Adaptation of HollowFlow to Attention</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As illustrated in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx69" title="" class="ltx_ref">69</a>]</cite>, attention can be considered a special case of message passing neural networks. Thus, the adaptation is straightforward, we outline two possible strategies in this section.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">First, we replace the general message function <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> (<a href="#S3.E14" title="In Permutation Equivariant Conditioner ‣ 3 Hollow Message Passing ‣ HollowFlow: Efficient Sample Likelihood Evaluation using Hollow Message Passing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>) by a product of the importance coefficients from a self-attention mechanism <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a:\mathbb{R}^{n_{h}}\times\mathbb{R}^{n_{h}}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a:\mathbb{R}^{n_{h}}\times\mathbb{R}^{n_{h}}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and a learnable function <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\phi}:\mathbb{R}^{n_{h}}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{n_{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\phi}:\mathbb{R}^{n_{h}}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{n_{h}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle m^{t}_{kij}=a(h^{t}_{ij},h^{t}_{ki})\tilde{\phi}(h^{t}_{ij}),\quad m^{t}_{ij}=\sum_{k\in\mathcal{N}^{lg}(i,j)}m^{t}_{kij},\quad h^{t+1}_{ij}=\psi(h^{t}_{ij},m^{t}_{ij})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle m^{t}_{kij}=a(h^{t}_{ij},h^{t}_{ki})\tilde{\phi}(h^{t}_{ij}),\quad m^{t}_{ij}=\sum_{k\in\mathcal{N}^{lg}(i,j)}m^{t}_{kij},\quad h^{t+1}_{ij}=\psi(h^{t}_{ij},m^{t}_{ij}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}^{lg}(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}^{lg}(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math> is defined in <a href="#A2.E28" title="In Notational remarks ‣ B.1 Hollowness of HollowFlow ‣ Appendix B Derivations and Proofs ‣ HollowFlow: Efficient Sample Likelihood Evaluation using Hollow Message Passing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Second, for graph-attention-like mechanism <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bibx70" title="" class="ltx_ref">70</a>]</cite>, we define the line graph softmax function for a graph <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>G</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{q}</annotation></semantics></math> with the corresponding notion of nearest neighbors <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}^{lg,q}(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}^{lg,q}(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{softmax}^{q}_{ij}(y_{ijk})=\frac{\exp\left(y_{ijk}\right)}{\sum_{l\in\mathcal{N}^{lg,q}(i,j)}\exp\left(y_{ijl}\right)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mtext>softmax</mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{softmax}^{q}_{ij}(y_{ijk})=\frac{\exp\left(y_{ijk}\right)}{\sum_{l\in\mathcal{N}^{lg,q}(i,j)}\exp\left(y_{ijl}\right)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">The updates of HollowFlow then become</p>
<table id="A1.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\alpha^{t,q}_{kij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\alpha^{t,q}_{kij}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{softmax}^{q}_{ij}(a(h^{t}_{ij},h^{t}_{ki}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mtext>softmax</mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{softmax}^{q}_{ij}(a(h^{t}_{ij},h^{t}_{ki}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h_{ij}^{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h_{ij}^{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma\left(\sum_{k\in\mathcal{N}^{lg,q}(i,j)}\alpha^{t,q}_{kij}\mathbf{W}_{ij}h^{t}_{ki}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma\left(\sum_{k\in\mathcal{N}^{lg,q}(i,j)}\alpha^{t,q}_{kij}\mathbf{W}_{ij}h^{t}_{ki}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}_{ij}\in\mathbb{R}^{n_{h}\times n_{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}_{ij}\in\mathbb{R}^{n_{h}\times n_{h}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a learnable weight matrix, <math id="A1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma:\mathbb{R}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma:\mathbb{R}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is a nonlinearity (applied element wise) and <math id="A1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a:\mathbb{R}^{n_{h}}\times\mathbb{R}^{n_{h}}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a:\mathbb{R}^{n_{h}}\times\mathbb{R}^{n_{h}}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is a non-linear self-attention function, typically a feed-forward neural network. One can also generalize to multi-head attention by independently executing <a href="#A1.E24" title="In Appendix A Adaptation of HollowFlow to Attention ‣ HollowFlow: Efficient Sample Likelihood Evaluation using Hollow Message Passing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eqs.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a> and <a href="#A1.E25" title="Equation 25 ‣ Appendix A Adaptation of HollowFlow to Attention ‣ HollowFlow: Efficient Sample Likelihood Evaluation using Hollow Message Passing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>, possibly even on differently connected graphs <math id="A1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{G_{q}\}_{q=1}^{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{G_{q}\}_{q=1}^{H}</annotation></semantics></math> potentially circumventing expressiveness problems, and then concatenating the result:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\alpha^{t,q}_{kij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\alpha^{t,q}_{kij}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{softmax}^{q}_{ij}(a(\mathbf{W}^{q}h^{t}_{ij},\mathbf{W}^{q}h^{t}_{ki}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mtext>softmax</mtext><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{softmax}^{q}_{ij}(a(\mathbf{W}^{q}h^{t}_{ij},\mathbf{W}^{q}h^{t}_{ki}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle h_{ij}^{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle h_{ij}^{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\bigparallel_{q=1}^{H}\sigma\left(\sum_{k\in\mathcal{N}^{lg,q}(i,j)}\alpha^{t,q}_{kij}\mathbf{W}_{ij}^{q}h^{t}_{ki}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo fence="false" largeop="true" movablelimits="false" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bigparallel_{q=1}^{H}\sigma\left(\sum_{k\in\mathcal{N}^{lg,q}(i,j)}\alpha^{t,q}_{kij}\mathbf{W}_{ij}^{q}h^{t}_{ki}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.4" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}^{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>q</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}^{q}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{W}_{ij}^{q}\in\mathbb{R}^{n_{h}\times n_{h}\times H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi>q</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{W}_{ij}^{q}\in\mathbb{R}^{n_{h}\times n_{h}\times H}</annotation></semantics></math> are learnable weight matrices and <math id="A1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of attention heads.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">These formulations demonstrate that both self-attention and graph-attention layers can be integrated into HollowFlow without altering its block-hollow Jacobian structure, enabling efficient divergence computations within attention-based architectures.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Derivations and Proofs</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Hollowness of HollowFlow</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first reintroduce some notation and do then restate <a href="#alg1" title="In Euclidean Symmetries of Node Features: ‣ 3 Hollow Message Passing ‣ HollowFlow: Efficient Sample Likelihood Evaluation using Hollow Message Passing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Block-hollowness of HoMP). ‣ Euclidean Symmetries of Node Features: ‣ 3 Hollow Message Passing ‣ HollowFlow: Efficient Sample Likelihood Evaluation using Hollow Message Passing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and proof it.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Notational remarks</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}^{lg}(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}^{lg}(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(i)</annotation></semantics></math> we mean the following notions of nearest neighbors:</p>
<table id="A2.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{N}^{lg}(i,j)=\{k|(k,i,j)\in E^{lg}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{N}^{lg}(i,j)=\{k|(k,i,j)\in E^{lg}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{N}(i)=\{k|(k,i)\in E\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{N}(i)=\{k|(k,i)\in E\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A2.E28" title="In Notational remarks ‣ B.1 Hollowness of HollowFlow ‣ Appendix B Derivations and Proofs ‣ HollowFlow: Efficient Sample Likelihood Evaluation using Hollow Message Passing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a> is illustrated in <a href="#A2.F4" title="In Notational remarks ‣ B.1 Hollowness of HollowFlow ‣ Appendix B Derivations and Proofs ‣ HollowFlow: Efficient Sample Likelihood Evaluation using Hollow Message Passing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. The functions <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi,\tilde{\phi},\psi,\tilde{\psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>ψ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi,\tilde{\phi},\psi,\tilde{\psi}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> used in <a href="#alg1" title="In Euclidean Symmetries of Node Features: ‣ 3 Hollow Message Passing ‣ HollowFlow: Efficient Sample Likelihood Evaluation using Hollow Message Passing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> are all learnable functions. <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B(t)\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B(t)\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> is the three-dimensional time-dependent back tracking array (see <a href="#S3.E16" title="In Permutation Equivariant Conditioner ‣ 3 Hollow Message Passing ‣ HollowFlow: Efficient Sample Likelihood Evaluation using Hollow Message Passing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a> and <a href="#alg1" title="In Euclidean Symmetries of Node Features: ‣ 3 Hollow Message Passing ‣ HollowFlow: Efficient Sample Likelihood Evaluation using Hollow Message Passing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), the integer <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> indicates the current message passing step. The binary variable <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{pd}\in\{true,false\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>pd</mtext><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{pd}\in\{true,false\}</annotation></semantics></math> indicated whether the algorithms runs on the (translation invariant) pairwise differences or not. The <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{detach}()" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">detach</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{detach}()</annotation></semantics></math> method means that derivatives w.r.t. the detached variable are ignored (i.e., equal to zero).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F4" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.21542v1/LG_N.svg" id="A2.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:238/131;" width="238" height="131"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 4</span>: </span><span id="A2.F4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Schematic example of the graph <math id="A2.F4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> (in blue) and its line graph <math id="A2.F4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(G)</annotation></semantics></math> (in orange)<span id="A2.F4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: The line graph nodes encircled with a continuos red line correspond to <math id="A2.F4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}^{lg}(j,i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}^{lg}(j,i)</annotation></semantics></math> while the node encircled with a dashed red line corresponds to <math id="A2.F4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}^{lg}(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}^{lg}(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math>. Two edges of <math id="A2.F4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(G)</annotation></semantics></math> are labelled explicitly to illustrate our labelling convention.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="alg1a" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Hollow message passing</figcaption>
<div id="alg1a.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1a" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1a.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
                
                
              <math id="alg1.l1a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathbf{x}_{i},Z_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}\text{ where }\ \mathbf{x}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\text{ and }Z_{i}\in\mathbb{R},\quad\text{pd}\in\{true,false\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> where </mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mtext>pd</mtext><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathbf{x}_{i},Z_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}\text{ where }\ \mathbf{x}_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}\text{ and }Z_{i}\in\mathbb{R},\quad\text{pd}\in\{true,false\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2a" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2a.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
                
                
              <math id="alg1.l2a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{b_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n},\ b_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{b_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n},\ b_{i}\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3a" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3a.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg1.l3a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <span id="alg1.l3a.4" class="ltx_text">pd</span> <span id="alg1.l3a.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4a" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4a.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
                
                
                <math id="alg1.l4a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{ij}=\mathbf{x}_{i}-\mathbf{x}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{ij}=\mathbf{x}_{i}-\mathbf{x}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>,  <math id="alg1.l4a.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{ij}=\texttt{embed}(d_{ij},Z_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">embed</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{ij}=\texttt{embed}(d_{ij},Z_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5a" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5a.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg1.l5a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l6a" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6a.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
                
                
                <math id="alg1.l6a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{i}=\texttt{embed}(\mathbf{x}_{i},Z_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">embed</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{i}=\texttt{embed}(\mathbf{x}_{i},Z_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7a" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7a.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
                
                
              <span id="alg1.l7a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l7a.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l8a" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8a.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
                
                
              Calculate <math id="alg1.l8a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=(N,E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=(N,E)</annotation></semantics></math>, e.g., as a <math id="alg1.l8a.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>NN graph. Self-loops, i.e., <math id="alg1.l8a.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,i)\in E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,i)\in E</annotation></semantics></math> are prohibited.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9a" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9a.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
                
                
              Calculate the line graph <math id="alg1.l9a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L(G)=(N^{lg},E^{lg})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L(G)=(N^{lg},E^{lg})</annotation></semantics></math> and its node features <math id="alg1.l9a.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{lg}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{lg}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math>:

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10a" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l10a.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
                
                
              <math id="alg1.l10a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N^{lg}=E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N^{lg}=E</annotation></semantics></math>,  <math id="alg1.l10a.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="E^{lg}=\{(i,j,k)|(i,j)\in E,(j,k)\in E\text{ and }i\neq k\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>E</mi><mtext> and </mtext><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{lg}=\{(i,j,k)|(i,j)\in E,(j,k)\in E\text{ and }i\neq k\}</annotation></semantics></math>,  <math id="alg1.l10a.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{lg}_{ij}=\begin{cases}e_{ij}\ \text{if }\text{pd}\\
